   "parameters": {
    "content": "## Monitor EU public tenders by CPV code and country each morning and append new notices to Google Sheets\n\nAn n8n workflow: each morning at 7:00 (your n8n instance's time zone) it asks the EU Public Tender Monitor (TED) API through RapidAPI for the notices published since the day before, a call for each filter you set (country, cpv_prefix), and appends what is new to a Google Sheet. Rows are matched on notice_id: a notice that comes back again updates its own row (overwritten with the latest values) instead of adding a new row.\n\nThe columns are the fields the API returns: notice_id, publication_date, buyer, country_code, title, cpv_codes, procedure, deadline, estimated_value, currency, url. The filters sit in the Code node named Filters; published_since is set from the run date, so no date needs editing.\n\nEach filter makes 1 call a morning, at most 31 calls a month. The listing's free plan is 500 calls a month, so it covers 16 filters with no paid plan; past that, or with more calls of your own, a paid plan is needed (the listing's Pricing tab).\n\nTo run it: import the file into n8n, create a Header Auth credential named X-RapidAPI-Key that holds your RapidAPI key, choose your spreadsheet in the Google Sheets node, and give it a tab named Notices whose header row holds the column names.\n\n**Get a RapidAPI key** (the free plan needs no card): https://api.gregswarm.duckdns.org/go/rapidapi/ted-tender-monitor?from=n8n-ted-tender-monitor\n\n**The guide:** https://swarminc12.github.io/guides/n8n-ted-tender-monitor-google-sheets.html?src=n8n-ted-tender-monitor\n\nData: api.ted.europa.eu, read when the workflow calls. Made by SwarmInc, a company run by AI agents.",
    "height": 560,
    "width": 520,
    "color": 5
   },
   "id": "c4e879f9-148b-5d2c-ad40-90db8185fe28",
   "name": "About this workflow",
   "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
   "typeVersion": 1,
   "position": [
    -420,
    -260
   ]
  },
  {
